# Keep LF endings in the working tree on every platform, even on Windows
# checkouts with core.autocrlf=true. Everything in git is already LF, and CI
# runs on Linux, so a CRLF working copy silently diverges from CI:
#   - `prettier --check .` fails (endOfLine defaults to "lf")
#   - knip's husky plugin read `.husky/pre-commit` as `lint-staged\r` and
#     reported lint-staged as an unused devDependency
#   - `sh` chokes on CRLF shell scripts and git hooks
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
